# Code style

Keep in sync with `docs/code-style-preferences.md`.

Preferences, not build errors. Prefer format-on-save over a failing build.

## JSX / TSX

- Opening tag, content, and closing tag on separate lines. Self-closing (`<br />`) may stay one line.
- One simple attribute: keep the opening tag on one line.
- Two or more attributes, a dense tag, or a multiline value: stack attributes.
- Self-closing with attributes: one attribute per line, one indent.
- Stay in the editor viewport. Wrap long values (especially `className`).
- Wrapped attributes: closing quote and `>` on separate visual boundaries — not `...">`.
- `className`: 1–2 tokens on one line; 3+ tokens split across lines.
- Multiline `className`: attributes on separate lines, `className` first.

### Tailwind

- Class tokens are static string literals only (no runtime-built names). Multiline static strings are fine.

### Catalog chrome

- One radius for search controls: `rounded-full` (search field, Sort, chips, facet rows). Do not mix `rounded-md` selected rows with `rounded-full` fields.
- Selected/highlight uses primary `asgreen` `#257257` (text and/or soft fill). Site navy `sky` `#1b263b` is the dark UI chrome color (panels, dark CTAs, footers, scrims) — do not use near-black or a darker-than-navy stop and treat navy as the light end. `ink` `#0d1b2a` is body text only; never a selected fill or dark surface.

## Indentation

- Tabs, not spaces, except where the format requires spaces (YAML, etc.).
- Stay consistent inside a file.

## TS

- `if` / `else if` / `else` and `try` / `catch` / `finally`: each block on its own line (not `} else {`).
- No space before `(`: `if(...)`, `else if(...)`, `switch(...)`, `catch(...)`.
- Single quotes in TS. Escape apostrophes; do not switch the string to double quotes.
- JSX/HTML attributes keep double quotes.

## Delimiters

- Do not stack `{}` `()` `[]` on one line when it gets dense; newline + one indent.
- One indent per newline, not a jump of two.
- Fat-arrow: stacked `()` on the same arrow is OK.
- Fat-arrow in JSX `{ }`: put the whole arrow expression on a new indented line so `{` and `(` do not stack.

## TSX ternaries

- `?` and `:` each on their own line, one indent deeper than the wrapper.
- Condition stays on the wrapper's opening line: `{cond` then `?` / `:`.
- JSX attribute braces: start on a new line; wrap the ternary in `()`.
- No clean wrapper: wrap the whole ternary in `()`.
- Multiline: closing `}` or `)` on its own line, aligned with the opener. Do not glue `}` to the last operand.

```tsx
{submitting
	? 'Sending code…'
	: 'Send reset code'
}
```

- Extra `()` is optional when the ternary is already in clean JSX `{ }`.
- Find with search/regex. Never fix with a regex replace. Edit each hit so the closer matches its opener.

## Reuse / icons

- Extract repeated UI. Import an existing widget instead of copying markup.
- No raw `<svg>` in pages or HTML. Put SVG in `apps/web/src/components/icons/` with a `className` prop.
- Directional / action cues (follow common menu & link conventions):
	- `ArrowLeftIcon` / `ArrowRightIcon` (shafted) — route navigation (and result-list pager that changes page/query).
	- `ChevronLeftIcon` / `ChevronRightIcon` (shaftless) — in-place only: hierarchy de-drill/drill, and image-carousel slide. Never reuse for page navigation. Breadcrumb separators use a plain `/` character (not chevrons/carets), so drill cues stay reserved for hierarchy UI.
	- `CaretDownIcon` — open a dropdown / expand-collapse toggle (not left/right direction).
	- `PencilIcon` — in-place edit affordance only (tier toggle / field edit). Never on a control that navigates to another page; full-editor navigate uses `ArrowRightIcon` (e.g. PDP “Full edit”), not a second pencil.
	- Navigate chrome — pick **one** style per control by context (do not mix for the same job):
		- **Inline / in-text navigators** (a link inside a sentence, footer link list, glossary jump, “Sold by …”, cart-message “View cart”): traditional link — `text-sky underline underline-offset-2`. Underlines are fine here; no navigate arrow required.
		- **Separate controls** (standalone section-header action, buy-box secondary, filled/outline CTA — not inline prose): either a clear whole-card / contextual navigate surface, **or** a shafted navigate icon (`ArrowRightIcon` forward / `ArrowLeftIcon` back). Do **not** use bare underlined text that only pretends to be a button. Examples: section “View all” / “All categories” (text + `ArrowRight`), standalone PDP “View cart” under Add to cart (text + `ArrowRight`), Checkout / Shop products CTAs.
		- **Whole-card / contextual menu rows** (full-row hit target: Account menu Account / Your orders, category choose rows, `CatalogMenuLink`): the row surface is the navigate cue — **no** trailing `ArrowRight`. Do not force shafted arrows on every menu row.
		- **“Back” navigation** must roll back history (`router.back` / `history.back`) when same-origin history exists; use a safe fallback `href` only when there is no history to roll back. Prefer shared `BackLink` (leading `ArrowLeftIcon` + fallback `href`). Do not label a guessed parent URL as “Back …” without history rollback. Examples: “Back to account”, “Back to orders”, “Back to vendor”.
		- In-place actions that are not route navigation (Clear all, Mark all read, Show more, expand toggles) are not under this rule; keep their existing action chrome.
	- Product/image carousels: one job per control — image plane may be a navigate backdrop to the PDP; slide carets/dots only change the slide (stopPropagation). Use chevrons for slide, not shafted arrows.
	- No raw `←` `→` `›` glyphs or unnamed caret/chevron components; use the icons.
- Find inline `<svg>` with search. Move each hit into an icon widget by hand — no regex rewrite.
